<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">16 August in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 16 August, from 1513 to 1977.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1513 <span class="tih-ago">513 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Henry VIII's army routs French cavalry at the Battle of the Spurs</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">English and imperial troops put French cavalry to flight near Guinegate, the speed of their retreat giving the battle its name. Thérouanne surrendered days later.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1780 <span class="tih-ago">246 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Cornwallis routs the Americans at Camden</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">British forces under Lord Cornwallis shattered Horatio Gates's army at Camden, South Carolina. The defeat led to Nathanael Greene taking command in the south.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1819 <span class="tih-ago">207 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Cavalry attack a reform meeting at Peterloo</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Yeomanry and hussars charged a crowd of some 60,000 at St Peter's Field, Manchester, gathered to demand parliamentary reform. About 18 people died and hundreds were injured.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1896 <span class="tih-ago">130 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Gold is found on Bonanza Creek in the Klondike</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">George Carmack, Skookum Jim and Dawson Charlie struck gold on a tributary of the Klondike River in the Yukon. When news reached the south in 1897, some 100,000 people set out for the goldfields.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1977 <span class="tih-ago">49 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Elvis Presley dies at Graceland</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Elvis Presley was found dead at his Memphis home, aged 42. The 'King of Rock and Roll' had sold hundreds of millions of records and transformed popular music.</p></div></li></ol>
